    {
      "heading": "A new challenge at the gold line",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-25-2021-arc-2-thanh-hau-nguyen-climbs-to-twenty-seventh"
      ],
      "text": "The entry now named ảc reaches 16th at 69.17, up eleven places and 5.28 points on the midnight comparison. This is the same team ID the wire previously reported as Thanh Hau Nguyen at 63.89, not a new debut. The current roster lists andy2709, locbaop and thanhhau097a; that observation establishes the listed accounts, not when they joined or who produced the gain."
    },
    {
      "heading": "ARC Raiders feels the rising cutoff",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-26-0201-arc-2-nguyenthanhnan-enters-gold-as-line-rises",
        "wire-2026-10-26-0403-arc-2-bao-loc-pham-enters-gold"
      ],
      "text": "The observed provisional gold score line rises from 68.75 to 69.17. ARC Raiders is 17th at an unchanged 68.75, immediately outside that boundary. Overnight wires also recorded NguyenThanhNhan and Bao Loc Pham reaching 69.17 in earlier snapshots. The latest edition observation places ảc at 16th; those earlier reports describe stages of a moving boundary, rather than three exclusive claims to the same current position."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Tufa holds the summit",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "Tufa Labs remains first at 88.06, ahead of Yi-Chia Chen @ Fields Model at 84.72 and Domdolus Tolus at 82.08. Those three scores are unchanged on the edition comparison. The strongest overnight consequence is therefore at the gold boundary, rather than a reshuffle of the podium."
    },
    {
      "heading": "More movement down the field",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-25-1804-arc-2-arshjot-khehra-debuts-at-45th"
      ],
      "text": "Richard Freinschlag reaches 84th at 37.08, gaining 2.08 points and 23 places on the edition comparison. Sophie555 rises 115 places to 118th at 34.31. Arshjot Khehra is now 43rd at an unchanged 52.50; the wire’s earlier debut report placed that entry 45th. A better rank without a higher score is a different development from a new scoring gain."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Methods remain an open assignment",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "The editor requested evidence about public methods behind the entries previously reported as Thanh Hau Nguyen and Arshjot Khehra. The saved material establishes standings and roster accounts, but no verified recipe for their current scores. That research follow-up is carried: this bounded edition did not inspect new notebooks, repositories or discussions, and does not infer a method from scores or submission counts. Social and discussion research was not refreshed. Public medal bands remain provisional."
